$DATUM 107-06-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM An experimental procedure is illustrated for the preparation of
N-[4-(1-carbethoxy)piperidinyl]-4-nitrobenzenamine (entry 4):
1-Carbethoxy-4-piperidone (3.2g, 19 mmol), pnitroaniline (1.4g, 10 mmol)
and glacial acetic acid (3.6g, 60 mmol) were mixed in 1,2-dichloroethane
(45 mL). Sodium triacetoxyborohydride (6.0g, 28 mmol) was added to the
above solution and the reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature
under a nitrogen atmosphere for 18 h (GC analysis indicated a complete
reaction in addition to ca 20% ketone reduction). The reaction was
quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 and the product was extracted with
EtOAc (3 x 75 mL). The EtOAc extract was dried (MgSO4) and the solvent
was evaporated to give a yellow semi-solid (4.7g). The semi-solid was
washed with ether/hexane (7:3) to remove the piperidone and piperidol and
the solid was collected by filtration (pure by GC). The analytical sample
was obtained by recrystallization from EtOAc/hexane. Yellow solid, yield
1.75g, 60%. mp 172-174°C; FT-IR (KBr) 3327 (s), 3182 (w), 3097 (w), 2929
(w), 2870 (m), 2398 (m), 1679 (s), 1600 (s), 1546 (m), 1460 (s), 1387
(m), 1296 (s), 1234 (m), 1184 (m), 1144 (m). 1105 (s), 1033 (m), 937 (m);
