$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 3(S)-4-acetyl-1-benzyl-3-iso-propylpiperazin-2-one (6m).
To a 0 °C stirring suspension of L-valine methyl ester hydrochloride (151
mg, 0.901 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular sieves (250 mg),
acetic acid (150 μL, 2.70 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (286 mg, 1.35 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile
solution of aldehyde 4a (189 mg, 0.99 mmol, 1.1 equiv.). After stirring
for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to
ambient temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The reaction was heated to
reflux for 24 hours, cooled and poured into aqueous saturated NaHCO3,
which was extracted three times with dichloromethane. The combined
organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by flash chromatography (2% methanol in dichloromethane)
provided piperazinone 6m as a clear oil (143 mg, 58% yield). Chiral HPLC
analysis (Chiralcel OD column 250 X 4.6 mm; 220 nm; flow = 1.0 mL/minute
of A/B:90/10 (A=hexanes, B=ethanol); 30 minute run. 86% enantiomeric
excess. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) (Rotamer A:B; 2:1) Rotamer A: δ 7.37-7.26
(m, 3H), 7.26-7.24 (m, 2H), 4.94 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.23 (d, J = 14.4
Hz, 1H), 4.07 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 3.77-3.69 (m, 1H), 3.36-3.29 (m, 1H),
3.17 (ddd, J = 12.2, 4.4, 2.9 Hz, 1H), 3.07 (ddd, J = 13.7, 10.7, 4.6 Hz,
1H), 2.34- 2.26 (m, 1H), 2.13 (s, 3H), 1.21 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H), 1.04 (d,
J = 7.1 Hz, 3H); Rotamer B: δ 7.37-7.26 (m, 3H), 7.26-7.24 (m, 2H), 5.00
(d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H), 4.82 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.42 (d, J = 14.6 Hz,
1H), 3.57 (ddd, J = 14.4, 10.5, 4.15 Hz, 1H), 3.36-3.29 (m, 1H), 3.21
(dt, J = 12.2, 3.6 Hz, 1H), 2.41-2.34 (m, 1H), 2.12 (s, 3H), 1.13 (d, J =
6.8 Hz, 3H), 1.00 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H). HRMS (ES) exact mass calculated
for C16H23N2O2 (M+H+): 275.1754; found 275.1256.Retention time for 6m =
17.4 minutes (Area % = 85.0), enantiomer retention time = 15.3 minutes
(Area % = 6.7);
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
