$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM tert-Butyl N-{[2-methoxy-4-(prop-2-yn-1-yloxy)phenyl]methyl}carbamate
(16). To a stirred solution of 2-methoxy-4-hydroxybenzaldehyde 15 (1.0 g,
6.6 mmol) and tert-butyl carbamate (2.3 g, 19.7 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (15 mL)
and acetonitrile (40 mL) at 20°C was added triethylsilane (3.15 mL, 19.7
mmol) followed, dropwise, by trifluoroacetic acid (1.0 mL, 13 mmol). The
mixture was stirred at 20°C for 18 h then partitioned between saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 (100 mL) and CH2Cl2 (2 x 50 mL). The combined organic
extracts were dried (MgSO4) and evaporated in vacuo to give an oil.
Chromatography of the residue (SiO2, 33% EtOAc in petrol) gave tert-butyl
N-[(4-hydroxy-2-methoxyphenyl)methyl]carbamate. A mixture of this
material with potassium carbonate (1.7 g, 12.3 mmol) and
3-bromo-1-propyne (80% in toluene, 2.4 mL, 25 mmol) in acetonitrile (30
mL) was stirred at 70°C for 5 h. Resulting mixture was cooled then
partitioned between water (50 mL) and EtOAc (50 mL), then the organic
phase was dried (Na2SO4) and evaporated in vacuo. Chromatography of the
residue (SiO2, 20% EtOAc in petrol). The title compound (1.1 g, 57% over
2 steps) as an oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6): 7.11 (1H, t), 7.04 (1H,
d), 6.58 (1H, d), 6.54 (1H, dd), 4.78 (2H, d), 4.02 (2H, d), 3.77 (3H,
s), 3.56 (1H, t), 1.39 (9H, s).
