$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure of reductive amination using
NaBH(OAc)3/DCE.
trans-Adamantane-2-spiro-3'-8'-[(2'-thiazolylamino)methyl]-1',2',4'-trioxaspiro[4.5]decane
(11). A mixture of 9 (292 mg, 1.0 mmol), 2-aminothiazole (150 mg, 1.5
mmol), acetic acid (240 mg, 4.0 mmol), CH2Cl2 (10 ml) and C1 CH2CH2Cl (10
rnl) was stirred for 2.5 h at rt before sodium triacetoxyborohydride (422
mg, 2.0 mmol) was added. The resulting mixture was stirred overnight and
then quenched with saturated sodium bicarbonate (50 rnl). The organic
layer was separated and washed with water, brine, dried over MgSO4 and
concentrated. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography
(silica gel, CH2Cl2/MeOH, 50: 1). The enriched product was dissolved in
CH2Cl2/ether (1:4, 20 ml) and methanesulfonic acid (40 mg, 0.4 rnrnol)
was added. The mixture was cooled to -20 °C overnight. The solvent was
decanted and the residue was washed with ether, dissolved in CH2Cl2 and
dried in vacuo to afford 11, yield 110 mg, 23%, as colorless solid.
cis-Adamantane-2-spiro-3'-8'-[(3'-oxo-1'-piperazinyl)methyl]-1',2',4'-trioxaspiro[4.5]decane
(13), colorless solid, yield 56% . mp 157 °C dec;1H NMR (CDCl3)δ1.07-1.25
(m, 2H), 1.41-2.05 (m, 21H), 2.17-2.27 (m, 2H), 2.61 (br s, 2H),
3.03-3.15 (m, 2H),3.35 (br s, 2H), 6.55 (br s, 1H); 13C (CDCl3)δ26.5,
26.9, 28.4, 33.6, 33.9, 34.76, 34.77,36.4, 36.8, 41.3, 49.7, 57.2, 63.4,
108.9, 111.3, 169.8. Anal. Calcd for C21H32N2O4: C, 66.99; H,8.57; N,
7.44. Found: C, 66.78; H, 8.51; N, 7.46.
