$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-Benzyloxymethyl-7-({benzyl[(2R/S,3S/R)-3,4-dihydroxy-2-(hydroxymethyl)butyl]amino}methyl)-4-methoxy-5H-pyrrolo[3,2-
d]pyrimidine (69). To a solution of (±)-67 (250 mg, 1.11 mmol) and
compound 44 8 (330 mg, 1.11 mmol) in MeOH (11 mL) was added acetyl
chloride (40 μL, 0.56 mmol), and this was followed by the addition of
sodium cyanoborohydride (105 mg, 1.67 mmol). The mixture was stirred at
room temperature for 72 h and then diluted with CH2Cl2, washed with
aqueous saturated NaHCO3 solution, dried, filtered, and the filtrate
concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was purified by
chromatography (7 M NH3 in MeOH/CH2Cl2 = 4:96) to afford (±)-69 (310 mg,
55%) as an immobile syrup. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 8.56 (s, 1H), 7.46-7.17 (m,
11H), 5.74 (s, 2H), 5.33 (s, 2H), 4.14 (s, 3H), 4.05 (d, J =14.2 Hz, 1H),
3.92 (d, J =14.2 Hz, 1H), 3.80-3.41 (m, 7H), 2.90 (dd, J = 13.2, 9.0 Hz,
1H), 2.72 (dd, J = 12.9, 5.1 Hz, 1H), 2.38 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ
156.9, 150.9, 150.7, 138.0, 137.2, 133.5, 129.7, 129.0, 128.9, 128.4,
128.0, 127.9, 112.3, 77.2, 74.3, 70.7, 65.1, 64.5, 59.4, 54.3, 54.1,
46.0, 40.9. ESI-HRMS for C28H35N4O5 [MH+] calcd, 507.2607; found,
507.2592.
