$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Methyl [2(S)-1-acetyl-4-benzyl-3-oxopiperazin-2-yl]acetate
(6l). To a 0 °C stirring suspension of L-aspartate dimethyl ester
hydrochloride (100 mg, 0.506 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular
sieves (200 mg), acetic acid (87 μL, 1.52 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (161 mg, 0.759 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile
solution of aldehyde 4a (106 mg, 0.557 mmol, 1.1 equiv.). After stirring
for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to
ambient temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The reaction was heated to
reflux for 10 hours, cooled and poured into aqueous saturated NaHCO3,
which was extracted three times with dichloromethane. The combined
organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by flash chromatography (0-15% ethyl acetate in
dichloromethane) provided piperazinone 6l as a clear oil (83 mg, 54%
yield). Chiral HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OD column 250 X 4.6 mm; 220 nm;
flow = 1.0 mL/minute of A/B:80/20 (A=hexanes, B=ethanol); 20 minute run.
82% enantiomeric excess. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) (Rotamer A:B; 1.5:1)
Rotamer A: δ 7.38-7.33 (m, 2H), 7.33-7.27 (m, 2H), 7.26-7.13 (m, 1H),
5.07 (t, J = 4.6 Hz, 1H), 4.80 (d, J = 14.9 Hz, 1H), 4.53 (d, J = 15.4
Hz, 1H), 3.94 (td, J = 11.1, 3.3 Hz, 1H), 3.78-3.68 (m, 1H), 3.68 (s,
3H), 3.44-3.32 (m, 1H), 3.30-3.18 (m, 1H), 3.13-2.97 (m, 2H), 2.10 (s,
3H); Rotamer B: δ 7.38-7.33 (m, 2H), 7.33-7.27 (m, 2H), 7.26-7.13 (m,
1H), 4.89 (t, J = 5.6 Hz, 1H), 4.85 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.66 (dd, J =
10.8, 3.7 Hz, 1H), 4.33 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.78-3.68 (m, 1H), 3.73 (s,
3H), 3.44-3.32 (m, 1H), 3.30-3.18 (m, 1H), 3.13-2.97 (m, 1H), 2.22 (s,
3H). HRMS (ES) exact mass calculated for C16H21N2O4 (M+H+): 305.1496;
found 305.1481. Retention time for 6l = 16.4 minutes (Area % = 73.6),
enantiomer retention time = 14.2 minutes (Area % = 7.2);
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
