$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (17)N-(2-methoxyethyl)-N-(1-((7-methy1H-indo3-yl)methyl)pyrrolidin-3-yl)methanesulfonamide(13).
Yield: 53% 7-methy1H-indole-3-carbaldehyde (65 mg,0.41 mmol) and
N-(2-methoxyethyl)-N-(pyrrolidin-3-yl)methanesulfonamide (91 mg, 0.41
mmol) was taken in DCE (3 mL). Few drops of acetic acid was added and
allowed to heat at 60 °C for 1hr. The reaction mixture was allowed to
cool and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (113 mg, 0.53 mmol) was added and
the resulting reaction mass was allowed to stiratroom temperature for
overnight. After the completion of the reaction, the volatiles were
removed and the residue was partitioned between saturated sodium
bicarbonate solution and ethyl acetate. The organic portion was washed
with water and brine solution, dried over sodium sulphate and evaporated
under vacuum to give crude compound which was purified by reverse phase
purification system to give
N-(2-methoxyethyl)-N-(1-((7-methy1H-indo3-yl)methyl)pyrrolidin-3-yl)methanesulfonamide.
Yield (80 mg, 53 %). 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ ppm 2.05 - 2.23 (m, 2H),
2.44 (s, 3H), 2.67 - 2.82 (m, 2H), 2.87 (s, 3H), 3.17 (s, 3H), 3.32 (br.
s., 3 H), 3.36 - 3.48 (m, 3H), 3.68 (s, 2H), 4.18 - 4.36 (m, 1H), 6.80 -
6.95 (m, 2H), 7.20 (d, J = 2.07 Hz, 1H), 7.43 (dd, J = 6.40, 2.64 Hz,
1H), 10.87 (s, 1H) HRMS: m/z (ES+) = 366.18455 (MH+) for C18H27N3O3S.
