$DATUM 75-05-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 4-acetyl-1-benzylpiperazin-2-one (6h). To a 0 °C stirring
suspension of glycine methyl ester hydrochloride (75 mg, 0.60 mmol, 1.0
equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular sieves (200 mg), acetic acid (100 μL, 1.79
mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (190 mg, 0.896 mmol,
1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5
mL acetonitrile solution of aldehyde 4a (123 mg, 0.643 mmol, 1.2 equiv.).
After stirring for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction
was warmed to ambient temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The reaction
was heated to reflux for 1 hour, cooled and poured into aqueous saturated
NaHCO3, which was extracted three times with dichloromethane. The
combined organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated
in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography (0 to 5% methanol in ethyl
acetate) provided piperazinone 6h as clear oil (73 mg, 53% yield). 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) (Rotamer A:B; 2:1) Rotamer A: δ 7.38-7.28 (m, 3H),
7.26-7.13 (m, 2H), 4.62 (s, 2H), 4.20 (s, 2H), 3.76 (t, J = 5.5 Hz, 2H),
3.27 (t, J = 5.4 Hz, 2H), 2.10 (s, 3H): Rotamer B: δ 7.38-7.28 (m, 3H),
7.26-7.13 (m, 2H), 4.63 (s, 2H), 4.31 (s, 2H), 3.62 (t, J = 5.3 Hz, 2H),
3.38 (t, J = 4.9 Hz, 2H), 2.07 (s, 3H). HRMS (ES) exact mass calculated
for C13H17N2O2 (M+H+): 233.1285; found 233.1279.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Substituted Piperazinones via Tandem Reductive
Amination-(N,N'-Acyl Transfer)-Cyclization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Beshore, Douglas C.; Dinsmore, Christopher J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(7), 1201-1204

