$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Oxoethyl 2,3,4,6-Tetra-O-acetyl-a-D-mannopyranoside (4) A solution of 1
(216 mg, 0.98 mmol) in pyridine (5 mL) was treated with acetic anhydride
(0.5 mL) overnight. The solution was evaporated and coevaporated with
toluene (3 x 100 mL) and dried at high vacuum. The obtained syrup was
dissolved in dry CH2Cl2 (20 mL), cooled to -78 °C and submitted to
ozonolysis for 15 min until the color of the solution turned blue. Then,
N2 was bubbled through the solution for 10 min, dimethyl sulfide (1.5 mL,
20.5 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred for 3 days at
r.t. When no peroxides could be detected, the solvent was removed in
vacuo and the residual crude product was purified on silica gel
(toluene/EtOAc, 1:1) to yield 4. Colorless syrup, yield 300 mg, 79%. [α]D
+50.6° (c 1.0, CHCl3). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 9.72 (s, 1H, CHO),
5.36-5.42 (m, 2H, H-3, H-2), 5.30 (dd~t, 1H, J = 9.7 Hz, H-4), 4.89 (d,
1H, J1,2 = 1.5 Hz, H-1), 4.23-4.30 (m, 3H, H-6, OCH2CHO), 4.09-4.14 (m,
2H, H-5, H-6'), 2.16, 2.10, 2.06, 2.01 (each s, each 3H, 4 OAc).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
