$DATUM 5-Benzyloxymethyl-7-({benzyl[(2R/S,3R/S)-3,4-dihydroxy-2-
(hydroxymethyl)butyl]amino}methyl)-4-methoxy-5H-pyrrolo[3,2- d]pyrimidine
(68). Acetyl chloride (21 μL, 0.30 mmol), compound 44 8 (179 mg, 0.60
mmol), compound (±)-66 (136 mg, 0.60 mmol), and sodium cyanoborohydride
(57 mg, 0.90 mmol) were successively added to MeOH (6 mL) and the
resulting reaction mixture stirred at room temperature for 64 h. The
mixture was concentrated in vacuo and the residue purified by
chromatography (CH2Cl2/7 M NH3 in MeOH = 96:4) to afford (±)-68 (159 mg,
52%) as a colorless gum. 1H NMR (CD3OD): δ 8.43 (s, 1H), 7.58 (s, 1H),
7.32-7.12 (m, 10H), 5.75 (s, 2H), 4.50 (s, 2H), 4.10 (s, 3H), 3.85 (s,
2H), 3.71 (dd, J = 10.9, 4.8 Hz, 1H), 3.65-3.51 (m, 4H), 3.48-3.37 (m,
2H), 2.69-2.57 (m, 2H), 2.19 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (CD3OD, center line at δ
49.0): δ 157.9, 151.3, 150.9, 139.8, 138.7, 135.1, 130.4, 129.3, 128.7,
128.6, 128.2, 116.8, 114.2, 78.6, 74.1, 71.6, 65.4, 63.7, 59.9, 55.5,
54.3, 48.5, 42.1. ESI-HRMS for C28H35N4O5 [MH+] calcd, 507.2607; found,
507.2604.
