$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(4S)-4-N-tert-Butoxycarbonylamino-5-(2-[N-tert-butoxycarbonylaminoethyl]aminopentyl]-N'-nitroguanidine
(13a). To a solution of 11 (303 mg, 1 mmol) in dry methanol, N
α-tert-butoxycarbonyl-1,2-ethanediamine (12, n = 1; 184 μL, 1 mmol) and 3
Å molecular sieves were added, and the mixture was stirred at room
temperature. After being stirred for 1 h, the reaction mixture was
treated with sodium triacetoxyborohydride (334.6 mg, 1.5 mmol) and
stirred overnight. The reaction mixture was filtered, and the filtrate
was concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by flash column
chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc/MeOH = 1:1).
(4S)-4-N-tert-Butoxycarbonylamino-5-(2-[N-tert-butoxycarbonylaminopropyl]aminopentyl]-N'-nitroguanidine
(13b). This compound (234 mg, 51%) was prepared as described above using
N α-tert-butoxycarbonyl-1,3-propanediamine (12b, n = 2): 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 4.90 (m, 1H), 3.69 (m, 1H), 3.18-3.21 (m, 4H), 2.77(m, 2H), 2.64
(m, 2H), 1.50-1.65 (m, 6H), 1.44 (brs, 18H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used,stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reduced Amide Bond Peptidomimetics.
(4S)-N-(4-Amino-5-[aminoalkyl]aminopentyl)-N'-nitroguanidines, Potent and
Highly Selective Inhibitors of Neuronal Nitric Oxide Synthase
