$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: o -Ph2P-C6H4-CH2NHC4H9 (1) The
o-aminophosphine ligands were synthesized by one-pot reductive amination
from the corresponding amine and aldehyde as shown in Scheme 1 [25]. The
2-(diphenylphosphine)-benzaldehyde (1.3 mmol) and the required amount of
the appropriate amine RNH2 were dissolved in 35 mL of CH2Cl2 in a 125 mL
Erlenmeyer flask. The sodium triacetoxyborohydride (approximately 2.0
mmol, 2 equivalents) was then added to the solution. When the reaction
was complete, the remaining borohydride was destroyed by the addition of
25 ml aqueous 5% sodium bicarbonate solution. After the foam subsided,
the solution was placed into a separatory funnel and the aqueous layer
was removed. The organic layer was washed twice more with 20-mL portions
of water. The solvent was removed by evaporation using a rotary
evaporator. The resulting solid was then recrystallized by dissolution in
hot ethanol (95%) until a homogeneous solution was obtained. While
keeping the solution hot, room temperature water was added dropwise with
agitation until the solution became turbid. At this point a few more
drops of ethanol were added to redissolve the precipitate. The flak was
cooled to room temperature, and then in an ice bath until the
precipitation was complete. The solid was collected and washed with a
small amount of ice ethanol. o -Ph2P-C6H4-CH2NHC12H25 (3) The synthesis
followed the method described for ligand 1 with a yield of 50%. FTIR
(KBr, cm-1): V(C-H): 2922, 2852, V(Ph-H): 3053, V(N-H): 3433. 31P(1H)-NMR
(CDCl3, δ ppm): -15.7. 1H NMR (CDCl3, δ ppm): 0.88 (3H, -CH3), 2.60 (1H,
-NH-), 4.19 (2H, PhCH2N-), 7.20-7.73 (14H, C6H5 and C6H4). 13C-NMR
(CDCl3, δ ppm): 14.1 (CH3), 51.8 (PhCH2N-), 127-136 (C6H5 and C6H4). MS
(ESI): m/z 460.3 (M + H+, 100).
