$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 8-phenethyl-8-azabicyclo[3.2.1]octan-3α-yl benzoate hydrochloride (4)
Freshly grinded NaBH(OAc)3 (400 mg, 1.9 mmol) was added to a round bottom
flask containing the free base of 8-azabicyclo[3.2.1]octan-3α-yl benzoate
(1) (290 mg, 1.3 mmol) and phenylacetaldehyde (170 μL, 90%, 1.3 mmol)
dissolved in DCE (5 mL). The mixture was stirred overnight at room
temperature under an atmosphere of nitrogen. Saturated NaHCO3 solution (5
mL) was added and the mixture was extracted with DCM (2 x 5 mL). The
combined organics were washed with NaHCO3(sat) (5 mL) and dried with
MgSO4. Concentration in vacuo afforded 331 mg of colorless oil. The crude
product was dissolved in Et2O (5 ml) and 5 ml of a 2M HCl solution in
Et2O was added dropwise. A white precipitate formed that was isolated by
decantation. The residue was washed with Et2O (2 x 10 ml) and
recrystalized from abs. EtOH. 232 mg (50%) of a white cubic shaped
crystals. Mp: decomposes and turns darker > 280 °C; 1H NMR (250 MHz,
MeOD) δ (ppm) 8.06 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.67 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 7.55
(t, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H), 7.44 - 7.25 (m, 5H), 5.37 (s, 1H), 4.14 (s, 2H),
3.34 (bs, 2H), 3.23 - 3.07 (m, 2H), 2.83 - 1.96 (m, 8H); 13C NMR (50 MHz,
MeOD) δ (ppm) 166.83, 137.71, 134.65, 131.23, 130.48, 130.02, 129.87,
128.34, 66.64, 32.21, 25.44; HRMS (m/z): [M+H]+ calcd. for C22H26NO2,
336.1958; found, 336.1955.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
