$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
products 8 and 9 In 15 cm3 dichloromethane 1.5 g
2-(6-bromoimidazo[1,2-a]-pyridin-2-yl or -3-yl)ethanamine (6.2 mmol), 1.4
g acetaldehyde (31 mmol) and 6.6 g NaBH(OAc)3 (31 mmol) were stirred at
room temperature under inert atmosphere for 24 h. The reaction mixture
was quenched by adding 20 cm3 aqueous 1 M NaOH and the product was
extracted with dichloromethane. The product was purified by
chromatography on silica gel using dichloromethane/methanol (95:5, v/v)
to afford oily products.
2-(6-Bromo-1H-imidazo[1,2-a]pyridin-3-yl)-N,N-diethylethanamine (9) Yield
72 %; 1-Acetyl-6-bromo-3-[2-(diethylamino)ethyl]imidazo[1,2-a]-pyridinium
acetate (9a), Yield 9% 9: Rf =0.6 (dichloromethane/methanol 85:15, v/v);
1H NMR (CDCl3): δ =1.10 (t, 6H, CH3 , J=7.1 Hz), 2.02 (s, 3H, CH3), 2.75
(q, 4H, NCH2, J=7.2 Hz), 2.92 (m, 2H, CH2), 3.10 (m, 2H, CH2), 7.21 (dd,
1H, H7 , J=9.5 Hz, 1.7 Hz), 7.42 (s, 1H, H2 ), 7.51 (d, 1H, H8, J=9.5
Hz), 8.06 (d, 1H, H5, J=1.0 Hz) ppm; 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ =10.3, 21.3,
22.5, 46.9, 50.3, 107.2, 118.3, 122.4, 123.8, 127.2, 131.5, 135.1, 143.8,
176.1 ppm. Rf =0.6 (dichloromethane/methanol 85:15, v/v); 1H NMR (CDCl3):
δ =1.10 (t, 6H, CH3 , J=7.1 Hz), 2.02 (s, 3H, CH3), 2.75 (q, 4H, NCH2,
J=7.2 Hz), 2.92 (m, 2H, CH2), 3.10 (m, 2H, CH2), 7.21 (dd, 1H, H7 , J=9.5
Hz, 1.7 Hz), 7.42 (s, 1H, H2), 7.51 (d, 1H, H8, J=9.5 Hz), 8.06 (d, 1H,
H5, J=1.0 Hz) ppm; 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ =10.3, 21.3, 22.5, 46.9, 50.3,
107.2, 118.3, 122.4, 123.8, 127.2, 131.5, 135.1, 143.8, 176.1 ppm.
