$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the preparation of products 8 and 9 In 15 cm3
dichloromethane 1.5 g 2-(6-bromoimidazo[1,2-a]-pyridin-2-yl or
-3-yl)ethanamine (6.2 mmol), 1.4 g acetaldehyde (31 mmol) and 6.6 g
NaBH(OAc)3 (31 mmol) were stirred at room temperature under inert
atmosphere for 24 h. The reaction mixture was quenched by adding 20 cm3
aqueous 1 M NaOH and the product was extracted with dichloromethane. The
product was purified by chromatography on silica gel using
dichloromethane/methanol (95:5, v/v) to afford oily products.
2-(6-Bromo-1H-imidazo[1,2-a]pyridin-2-yl)-N,N-diethylethanamine (8),
Yield 60 %; 8-Bromo-2-ethyl-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-1-methyldipyrido
[1,2-a:4',3'-d]imidazole (8a), yield 6% 8: C13H18BrN3. Rf =0.4
(dichloromethane/methanol 90:10, v/v); 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ =1.06 (t, 6H,
CH3, J=7.2 Hz), 2.65 (q, 4H, NCH2, J=7.2 Hz), 2.95 (m, 4H, CH2,NCH2),
7.13 (dd, 1H, H7 , J=9.6 Hz, 1.8 Hz), 7.36 (d, 1H, H8 , J=9.6 Hz), 7.39
(s, 1H, H3), 8.16 (dd, 1H, H5,J=1.8 Hz, 0.7 Hz) ppm; 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ
=11.4, 26.1, 46.8, 52.3, 106.4, 109.8, 117.4, 125.4, 127.4, 143.3, 146.7
ppm; MS (APCI+):m/z=296.0, 298.0 ([M+H]+ ). 8a: C13H16BrN3, Rf =0.6
(dichloromethane/methanol 90:10, v/v); 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ =1.11 (t, 3H,
CH3, J=7.1 Hz), 1.32 (d, 3H, CH3 , J=6.7 Hz), 2.62 (m, 3H, CH2), 2.96 (m,
2H, CH2), 3.09 (m, 1H, CH2), 4.05 (q, 1H, CH, J=6.7 Hz), 7.10 (dd, 1H,
H7, J=9.5 Hz, 1.8 Hz), 7.37 (d, 1H, H8 , J=9.5 Hz), 7.86 (d, 1H, H5 ,
J=1.1 Hz) ppm; 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ =13.3, 15.4, 22.8, 43.2, 46.9, 49.7,
106.3, 117.1, 122.6, 123.1, 126.4, 104.7, 142.9 ppm; MS (APCI+):
m/z=294.2, 296.2 ([M+H]+ ).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternatively reaction carried out using decreased amount of NaBH(OAc)3
gave 30% of 6-bromo-N,N-diethyl-imidazo[1,2-a]pyridine-2-ethanamine and
16% of
8-bromo-2-ethyl-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-1-methyl-pyrido[4',3':4,5]imidazo[1,2-a]pyridine,
Pictet-Spengler reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Exploring 6-(substituted sulfonyl)imidazopyridines as a potential
scaffold for the design of 5-HT6 ligands
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Heloire, Valeria Moas; Furman, Christophe; Melnyk, Patricia; Carato,
Pascal
