$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: One Step (Method B): A solution of alkene (~1
mmol) and MeOH (0.3 mL) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) in a round-bottomed flask was
ozonized as in GP 1. Following removal of free ozone, the cooling bath
was removed and NaBH(OAc)3 (3 mmol) and the amine (1-2 mmol) were
sequentially added. The reaction mixture was stirred at r.t. for 1-2 h
and then filtered through Celite and the pad washed with CH2Cl2 (20 mL).
The filtrate was concentrated on a rotary evaporator, and the residue was
purified as in GP 3. 9-(N-Morpholino)nonyl Acetate Ester (2d) Prepared
from 2a (0.099 g, 0.5 mmol) with morpholine (1 mmol) by GP 4B; reaction
time: 6 h. The product was identical to 2d obtained as above.
N-Benzylcyclohexylmethananiine (11a) [4352-47-0] and
N-benzyl-N-methylcyclohexylmethanamine (11b) [79952-95-7] Prepared from
the reaction of vinylcyclohexane (0.11 g, 1 mmol) with benzylamine (2
mmol) by GP 4B; reaction time: 6 h. The reaction also yielded 10% of 11b.
N-Benzylcyclohexylmethananiine (11a), yield: 0.102 g (50%);
N-benzyl-N-methylcyclohexylmethanamine (11b), 10% yield 11a: Rf= 0.50
(10% MeOH-CH2Cl2). 1H NMR: δ = 7.36-7.26 (m, 5 H), 3.80 (s, 2 H), 2.49
(d, J = 6.7 Hz, 2 H), 1.84-1.68 (m, 5 H), 1.57-1.46 (m, 1 H), 1.32-1.13
(m, 4 H), 0.99-0.90 (m, 2 H). 13C NMR: δ = 140.6, 128.4, 128.0, 126.8,
56.2, 54.1, 37.9, 31.5, 26.7, 26.1. 11b: Rf= 0.63 (10% MeOH-CH2Cl2). 1H
NMR (600 MHz): δ = 7.35-7.24 (m, 5 H), 3.47 (s, 2 H), 2.18-2.16 (m, 5 H),
1.84 (d, J = 12.4 Hz, 2 H), 1.74-1.67 (m, 3 H), 1.57-1.51 (m, 1 H),
1.28-1.13 (m, 3 H), 0.89-0.82 (m, 2 H). 13C NMR (150 MHz): δ = 139.8,
128.9, 128.0, 126.7, 64.7, 62.7, 42.9, 35.8, 31.8, 26.9, 26.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM gaseous O3(2%)/O2 used (1st stage)
